„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ5and Joiada begat Jonathan, and Jonathan begat Jaddua.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦versesš„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnAnd in the days of Joiakim were priests, the chief of the fathers: of Seraiah, Meraiah; of Jeremiah, Hananiah;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ*of Ezra, Meshullam; of Amariah, Jehohanan;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ*of Melicu, Jonathan; of Shebaniah, Joseph;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ$of Harim, Adna; of Meraioth, Helkai;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ,of Iddo, Zechariah; of Ginnethon, Meshullam;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ3of Abijah, Zichri; of Miniamin, of Moadiah, Piltai;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ,of Bilgah, Shammua; of Shemaiah, Jehonathan;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ+and of Joiarib, Mattenai; of Jedaiah, Uzzi;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ!of Sallai, Kallai; of Amok, Eber;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ-of Hilkiah, Hashabiah; of Jedaiah, Nethaneel.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŸThe Levites in the days of Eliashib, Joiada, and Johanan, and Jaddua, were recorded chief of the fathers: also the priests, to the reign of Darius the Persian.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹The sons of Levi, the chief of the fathers, were written in the book of the chronicles, even until the days of Johanan the son of Eliashib.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙåAnd the chief of the Levites: Hashabiah, Sherebiah, and Jeshua the son of Kadmiel, with their brethren over against them, to praise and to give thanks, according to the commandment of David the man of God, ward over against ward.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙzMattaniah, and Bakbukiah, Obadiah, Meshullam, Talmon, Akkub, were porters keeping the ward at the thresholds of the gates.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ–These were in the days of Joiakim the son of Jeshua, the son of Jozadak, and in the days of Nehemiah the governor, and of Ezra the priest, the scribe.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙöAnd at the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem they sought the Levites out of all their places, to bring them to Jerusalem, to keep the dedication with gladness, both with thanksgivings, and with singing, with cymbals, psalteries, and with harps.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“And the sons of the singers gathered themselves together, both out of the plain country round about Jerusalem, and from the villages of Netophathi;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹also from the house of Gilgal, and out of the fields of Geba and Azmaveth: for the singers had builded them villages round about Jerusalem.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjAnd the priests and the Levites purified themselves, and purified the people, and the gates, and the wall.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse%¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¸Then I brought up the princes of Judah upon the wall, and appointed two great companies of them that gave thanks, whereof one went on the right hand upon the wall toward the dung gate:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ?and after them went Hoshaiah, and half of the princes of Judah,¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ!and Azariah, Ezra, and Meshullam,¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ0Judah, and Benjamin, and Shemaiah, and Jeremiah,¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ»and certain of the priests' sons with trumpets; namely, Zechariah the son of Jonathan, the son of Shemaiah, the son of Mattaniah, the son of Michaiah, the son of Zaccur, the son of Asaph:¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙµand his brethren, Shemaiah, and Azarael, Milalai, Gilalai, Maai, Nethaneel, and Judah, Hanani, with the musical instruments of David the man of God, and Ezra the scribe before them.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÁAnd at the fountain gate, which was over against them, they went up by the stairs of the city of David, at the going up of the wall, above the house of David, even unto the water gate eastward.¦layout ªlast_verse%…¤book§chapter«first_verse&ªlast_verse+¦verses–„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÂAnd the other company of them that gave thanks went over against them, and I after them, and the half of the people upon the wall, from beyond the tower of the furnaces even unto the broad wall;¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÉand from above the gate of Ephraim, and above the old gate, and above the fish gate, and the tower of Hananeel, and the tower of Meah, even unto the sheep gate: and they stood still in the prison gate.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsSo stood the two companies of them that gave thanks in the house of God, and I, and the half of the rulers with me:¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙiand the priests; Eliakim, Maaseiah, Miniamin, Michaiah, Elioenai, Zechariah, and Hananiah, with trumpets;¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙand Maaseiah, and Shemaiah, and Eleazar, and Uzzi, and Jehohanan, and Malchijah, and Elam, and Ezer. And the singers sang loud, with Jezrahiah their overseer.¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÈAlso that day they offered great sacrifices, and rejoiced: for God had made them rejoice with great joy: the wives also and the children rejoiced: so that the joy of Jerusalem was heard even afar off.¦layout ªlast_verse+…¤book§chapter«first_verse,ªlast_verse/¦verses”„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ2And at that time were some appointed over the chambers for the treasures, for the offerings, for the firstfruits, and for the tithes, to gather into them out of the fields of the cities the portions of the law for the priests and Levites: for Judah rejoiced for the priests and for the Levites that waited.¦layout ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¡And both the singers and the porters kept the ward of their God, and the ward of the purification, according to the commandment of David, and of Solomon his son.¦layout ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyFor in the days of David and Asaph of old there were chief of the singers, and songs of praise and thanksgiving unto God.¦layout ªlast_verse.„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙıAnd all Israel in the days of Zerubbabel, and in the days of Nehemiah, gave the portions of the singers and the porters, every day his portion: and they sanctified holy things unto the Levites; and the Levites sanctified them unto the children of Aaron.¦layout ªlast_verse/